Packaging / PyPI (deferred from the 0.1.8 install-hygiene work, 2026-08-05)
- Ship py.typed (PEP 561). Currently absent, so downstream type checkers must
  discard our annotations. The blocker is NOT our ~458 internal mypy errors --
  measured: mypy does not report errors from site-packages, so zero of them
  reach a user (verified by installing a py.typed build and type-checking a
  small program against it). The blocker is that our *signatures* would then
  become authoritative, and some are wrong in ways that produce FALSE errors in
  correct user code. Two mechanical classes, both pure widenings with no
  runtime effect:
    * 79 implicit-Optional params (`x: np.ndarray = None` should be
      `Optional[np.ndarray] = None`); modern mypy reads the declared type as
      non-optional, so passing None is flagged.
    * 31 invariant `List[X]` params on public functions; `list` is invariant,
      so `Satellite(actuators=[MTQ(...), ...])` -- the README's own example --
      is reported as an error. Should be `Sequence[X]` where the body only
      reads. Check for mutation before converting.
  Fix those ~110 signatures, then add the marker and a mypy CI gate.
- requirements.txt is still a hand-maintained pinned environment that can drift
  from pyproject.toml (the junk `np==1.0.2` is gone and the file now documents
  its role, but nothing enforces consistency). CI installs it and never runs
  `pip install .`, so the pyproject dependency set is exercised only by the
  wheel smoke-test in publish.yml. Consider having CI install `.[dev]` instead.
- Add a TestPyPI dry-run to the release process. `twine check` only validates
  metadata rendering; it does not catch a wheel that installs but cannot
  import (which is how 0.1.5 shipped without cholesky_update.py). The wheel
  smoke-test job in .github/workflows/publish.yml covers most of this now.
- 0.1.5 will NOT be yanked (decided 2026-08-05). It installs and imports fine;
  only the SRUAKF fails, and once 0.1.8 is published pip resolves to that
  anyway. Yanking would mainly have affected people pinning ==0.1.5, who are
  exactly the people yanking does not help.
